  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 214 PM EDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nGuidance remains in good agreement showing high pressure dominating \nthe weather pattern and keeping things dry through day 7. North and \nCentral GA will remain dry in this setup, as primarily northerly \nflow keeps PWATs below 0.5\" and rain chances near zero. High \ntemperatures expected to remain mainly in the 70s through the period \nwith the warmest day Thu with highs getting to near 80 deg across \ncentral portions of the state. The models do show the overall flow \nswitching from the NW to E/NE Friday allowing a little bit of \nmoisture return across south and central GA Sat through Mon. Right \nnow the most we should see from this is some increased cloud cover \nbut that should be about it.",
